lue "CCS"} "Cross Country Skiing"] "\n" [:option {:value "FSK"} "Figure Skating"] "\n" [:option {:value "IHO"} "Ice Hockey"] "\n" [:option {:value "MSP"} "Military Ski Patrol"] "\n" [:option {:value "NCB"} "Nordic Combined"] "\n" [:option {:value "SKN"} "Skeleton"] "\n" [:option {:value "SJP"} "Ski Jumping"]]] [:script {} "$('#sports_in_same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/33/sports/'+$('#sports_in_same_games_select').val()})"] [:form {:id "other_games_form", :class "form-inline", :style "display: inline", :method "get"} [:select {:name "year", :id "sport_in_other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "Speed Skating in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "29"} "1924 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "30"} "1928 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "31"} "1932 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "32"} "1936 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "34"} "1952 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "35"} "1956 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "36"} "1960 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "37"} "1964 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "38"} "1968 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "39"} "1972 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "40"} "1976 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "41"} "1980 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "42"} "1984 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "43"} "1988 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "44"} "1992 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "45"} "1994 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "46"} "1998 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "47"} "2002 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "49"} "2006 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "57"} "2010 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "66"} "2012 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "58"} "2014 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "68"} "2016 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "60"} "2018 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "70"} "2020 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "62"} "2022 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "73"} "2024 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "72"} "2026 Winter Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/SSK'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Speed Skating at the 1948 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "31 January –  3 February 1948"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "4"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/144"} "Olympia-Eisstadion Badrutts Park, St. Moritz"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Just 20 years after it hosted its first Games, St. Moritz again hosted the Games. The " [:a {:href "/venues/144"} "same rink"] " as in 1928 was used. At an altitude of 1,856 m above sea level, it is the second-highest Olympic rink ever used, only second to that in " [:a {:href "/venues/138"} "Squaw Valley in 1960"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Due to the war, speed skating in Europe had come to a complete standstill, with the exception of neutral nations Sweden and Switzerland. This was visible from the results of the Scandinavians, which had not won any Olympic speed skating medal prior to 1948, but won three in St. Moritz. The war had also an influence on the entries, as both war aggressors Germany and Japan had been barred from competing in the first post-War Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Several of the Soviet Union’s top skaters were seen training in St. Moritz, but they did not participate in the Olympics. The Games were still considered too “bourgeois” by the country’s leaders, although negotiations took place in Switzerland in order to appear at the " [:a {:href "/editions/12"} "Summer Olympics in London"] ". While this failed to to yield results, the Soviets did decide to participate in the World Championships, held in Helsinki, where Konstantin Kudryavtsev won the 500 m. It would take until " [:a {:href "/editions/13"} "1952"] " for the Soviet Union to appear at the Summer Olympics, and until " [:a {:href "/editions/35"} "1956"] " for the Winter edition."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Three countries sent speed skaters to the Olympics for the first time. Italy had entered skaters at earlier occasions, but they had never actually competed. This time, four Azzurri participated. Another debutant was Denmark, which had entered " [:a {:href "/athletes/87686"} "Aage Justesen"] " as its sole contestant. Korea had sent three skaters for the nation’s Olympic début. They were not the first Korean speed skaters at the Olympics, as three of their compatriots had competed under the Japanese flag in " [:a {:href "/editions/32/sports/SSK"} "1936"] ", when the Korean peninsula was under Japanese rule at that time."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Before the first race, there was a protest lodged against the method of drawing pairs. Led by the Americans, nearly all participating nations joined the protest, save for the Scandinavians and the host nation. The rules stated that results of the races influenced the draw of the remaining races. This made sense for all-round competitions, but since the Olympics consisted of four separate races, the team leaders thought this rule to be illogical. However, the organization did not uphold the protest and the competitions were held as planned. The Americans again complained when this rule left all Americans competing in poor conditions during the " [:a {:href "/results/996"} "10,000 m"] ", but again without effect."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/993"} "500 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "31 January 1948"] "\n" 